# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by default. Only scripts/, the README figures in results/ and the files below are
# committed — nothing else leaves this machine.
#
# Everything else (notes/, docs/, literature/, reports/) stays on disk and
# works normally; it is simply never offered to git.
#
# NOTE: this governs UNTRACKED files only. The upstream simulator, devkit,
# Dockerfiles and graphics are already tracked and are unaffected. A NEW file
# under autodrive_devkit/ will be ignored — add an allow rule or `git add -f`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# Git must be able to descend into directories, or nothing inside one can be
# un-ignored. This permits traversal, not the files.
!*/

# --- the only things we commit ---------------------------------------------
!/scripts/*.py
!/scripts/*.sh
# The frozen Follow-the-Gap baselines: the one piece of data the committed code
# cannot work without. circuits.py reads it on import and raises without it, and
# every normalised score ever recorded is relative to these numbers. Measurement
# output, not notes -- the notebook and the experiment CSVs stay local.
!/data/baseline_ftg.csv
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
# The README's figures and the CSVs they were drawn from (scripts/plot_results.py).
!/results/*.svg
!/results/*.csv

# --- never, even if a rule above would otherwise allow it ------------------
# Listed last because the last matching rule wins.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
